From 74d6327123259dd6c6c80168555a8d7d022ec894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 4evy <git@evy.pink>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0300
Subject: git push: make sign-on-push accept a revset

Let users define signing policy with the same revset language used by other jj configuration. Intersect the configured selector with commits outgoing to the pushed references and force-sign exactly the selected commits.

Default to none() and migrate boolean values for six releases so existing configurations keep their old mutable, unsigned, own-commit behavior.

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 8b9746ad9cc24f65f9b790cde851c3d30b3cd2f6..a78138b2ba2dccb8741be00f6a80e9d665c9efac 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -83,6 +83,10 @@ published.
 * `jj git import` in non-colocated repositories no longer imports commits from a
   detached Git HEAD branch.
 
+* `git.sign-on-push` is now a revset selecting commits to sign instead of a
+  boolean. The default is `none()`. Existing `true` values are migrated to
+  `~signed() & mine()` and `false` values to `none()`.
+
 ### Deprecations
 
 None
